# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over a root `.dockerignore`.
#
# The Dockerfile copies the WHOLE repo, because `bun.lock` describes every workspace member and a
# partial copy makes `--frozen-lockfile` refuse. This file keeps that cheap — but it may only
# exclude things that are NOT workspace members. Excluding `examples/*/apps` removed those
# members' `package.json` files, which is the same refusal by another route: bun resolves the
# workspace from the manifests on disk, so a missing manifest is a lockfile that "changed".
#
# The rule: ignore artifacts and secrets, never a manifest.

# Members outside the demo's closure (its own members, and every framework package they import):
# each one's SOURCE goes — an edit to the reference app, the docs site, the wiki or a repo guard
# re-ran `COPY . .` and the prebuilt step under it, for a file no boot reads — and each MANIFEST is
# re-included, for the refusal above. Above `**/node_modules`, so that line, read later, still
# drops a host `node_modules/**/package.json` the re-include would otherwise match.
examples/**
!examples/**/package.json
dummy/docs-site/**
!dummy/docs-site/**/package.json
packages/create-ultimate/**
!packages/create-ultimate/package.json
scripts
wiki
.claude
.dz

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Artifacts. `.x/` holds the embedded Postgres data directory — hundreds of files, none of them
# meaningful in a container that talks to a real server.
**/.x
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage

# Tests run in CI, never in a container, and an edit to one would rerun every line below COPY . .
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
# Anchored: a package may hold a docs/ it reads at run time. The root is the framework's, the second
# line this app's: in this context its docs/ does not sit at the root.
docs
dummy/social-media-clone/docs

.git
.github

# Never bake an environment into an image: one artifact deploys everywhere and the values arrive
# from the platform.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Same shape, different file, and the one this list was missing: an `.npmrc` carries a registry auth
# token, so any that exists here is somebody's local credential. This Dockerfile is `COPY . .` over
# the WHOLE repo and `.github/workflows/deploy-social-demo.yml` builds it with
# `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max` — an untracked `.npmrc` on a contributor's box would land in a layer
# and be pushed to a cache the whole repository can read. The other three ignore files beside this
# one have carried the line since 2026-08-19.
**/.npmrc
# Same shape, and this one is the key itself: `.secrets.key` decrypts the committed
# `secrets.enc.json` beside it, and `findMasterKey` falls back to the file whenever
# ULTIMATE_SECRETS_KEY is unset — so a baked copy boots the image on it and the platform's key is
# never exercised.
**/.secrets.key
# the test-only TLS key the postgres-tls-certs one-shot writes (#519); never in a build context
docker/.tls
